WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.375 --> 00:00:02.460
♪♪♪
- [Adam Lefkoe:] When you speak, we listen.

00:00:02.460 --> 00:00:04.879
Move 'em! Move the cones! Let's do it.

00:00:05.463 --> 00:00:09.092
- [Alex DeBrincat:] They're really making this tough on me.
- Now we'll see what he's really got.

00:00:09.092 --> 00:00:11.970
♪♪♪
- [Lefkoe:] Booom!

00:00:15.807 --> 00:00:18.143
Woo! It is cold, and I feel good.

00:00:18.184 --> 00:00:19.310
Welcome to "Underrated."

00:00:19.310 --> 00:00:25.275
I'm Adam Lefkoe. Behind me is the Cat. Alex DeBrincat,
a young rising star

00:00:25.275 --> 00:00:29.487
for the Chicago Blackhawks, third-leading
scorer in the NHL last season.

00:00:29.696 --> 00:00:34.701
And we wanna know how he looks in NHL 22.
What X-factors does he bring?

00:00:34.909 --> 00:00:37.620
We got our pro gamer Nasher to take a look.

00:00:38.830 --> 00:00:39.748
- [Nasher:] What I'm looking for in

00:00:39.748 --> 00:00:43.209
a left winger is somebody that's speedie.
They can go up and down the ice.

00:00:43.209 --> 00:00:44.461
No problem at all.

00:00:44.461 --> 00:00:49.132
Make that move and not just score goals
but score nasty goals as well.

00:00:49.174 --> 00:00:51.593
And I feel like that's
what ADB does best.

00:00:51.593 --> 00:00:53.261
He's got "make it snappy."

00:00:53.261 --> 00:00:55.930
So he has the ability to just go up
and down the ice again.

00:00:55.930 --> 00:00:57.557
When you have those defenders
in front of you,

00:00:57.557 --> 00:00:59.726
you wanna be able
to quickly make that move.

00:00:59.726 --> 00:01:01.061
And he's the one that can do it.

00:01:06.524 --> 00:01:08.651
♪♪♪
- [Lefkoe:] When you were playing NHL games growing up,

00:01:08.651 --> 00:01:11.154
who was your team?
- Uhh.

00:01:11.154 --> 00:01:12.030
- Who was the squad?

00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:13.198
- Yeah, definitely Detroit.

00:01:13.198 --> 00:01:15.366
- [Lefkoe:] Red Wings.
- I was a huge Red Wings fan growing up.

00:01:15.366 --> 00:01:18.328
- And would you play a lot?
- Yeah, I like the NHL a lot. Yeah.

00:01:18.995 --> 00:01:22.040
- We just heard from our pro gamer
Nasher that you have

00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:24.834
a very important X-factor
that not everyone else has:

00:01:25.085 --> 00:01:30.298
"make it snappy," the ability
to get off that wrist shot super quick.

00:01:31.174 --> 00:01:34.761
I'm here today to make sure
that you still deserve it.

00:01:35.553 --> 00:01:37.555
So we've got a little defense set up here.

00:01:37.555 --> 00:01:38.765
And I mean little.

00:01:38.765 --> 00:01:42.393
We need you to skate through our defenders
and take a shot on goal.

00:01:42.685 --> 00:01:44.771
You get six chances to explode

00:01:44.854 --> 00:01:47.607
two of our targets.
You can get two of those things

00:01:47.607 --> 00:01:51.319
you've proven you deserve
the "make it snappy" X-factor.

00:01:51.319 --> 00:01:52.070
- All right.
- [Lefkoe:] You cool?

00:01:52.070 --> 00:01:52.821
- Yeah, yeah, it's cool.

00:01:53.154 --> 00:01:54.656
- The Cat is on the ice.

00:01:54.656 --> 00:01:57.158
Let's do it.
[Lefkoe making skating sound effect]

00:01:58.284 --> 00:02:00.411
All right, which target you going
for first?

00:02:00.411 --> 00:02:02.038
- [Alex DeBrincat:] I'm going for top left.
- [Lefkoe:] Top left?

00:02:02.038 --> 00:02:02.372
- [DeBrincat:] Yeah.

00:02:02.372 --> 00:02:06.543
- [Lefkoe:] In three, two, one.
[Whistle blowing]

00:02:06.543 --> 00:02:09.087
The Cat, weavin' in.

00:02:09.587 --> 00:02:11.756
Ooh, almost destroyed the goalie in the face.
[Buzzer]

00:02:13.383 --> 00:02:15.927
DeBrincat weaving… Woo!

00:02:17.762 --> 00:02:21.015
[Sighing] That was two inches…

00:02:21.015 --> 00:02:22.267
- [DeBrincat:] That's as close as you can get.
- Two inches.

00:02:23.726 --> 00:02:27.689
DeBrincat weaves in.
Booom!

00:02:27.689 --> 00:02:30.275
Bang. That's how it's done.

00:02:30.275 --> 00:02:33.111
Can’t you see? It's like I played hockey.
I knew you do a little knuckle.

00:02:33.820 --> 00:02:35.405
That felt good. How did it feel?

00:02:35.405 --> 00:02:37.282
- [DeBrincat:] That felt good. That felt good.
- [Lefkoe:] See?

00:02:37.282 --> 00:02:39.284
I think this should be hockey
all the time.

00:02:39.284 --> 00:02:41.619
- [DeBrincat laughing]
- [Lefkoe:] You score and confetti explodes.

00:02:41.619 --> 00:02:43.288
- [DeBrincat:] Yeah.
- [Lefkoe:] OK, there's one.

00:02:43.288 --> 00:02:44.330
- I'm going top right.

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:46.457
Yeah. That's probably good.
- [Lefkoe:] The man likes top shelf.

00:02:46.666 --> 00:02:48.835
All right, DeBrincat wants two.

00:02:48.835 --> 00:02:52.422
Let's make it snappy. Oh, the goalie is dead…
♪♪♪

00:02:56.342 --> 00:02:57.260
This is the last one.

00:02:57.260 --> 00:02:58.303
Whenever you're ready, man.

00:02:58.303 --> 00:03:01.639
- [DeBrincat:] All right.
- [Lefkoe:] You got this, bro.

00:03:02.891 --> 00:03:05.226
Here he goes. He has one.

00:03:05.226 --> 00:03:07.645
He needs the second one.
♪♪♪

00:03:11.983 --> 00:03:13.610
Boom! Nailed it!

00:03:13.610 --> 00:03:16.863
Not only did you nail it. Oh, man,
I'm proud of you.

00:03:17.071 --> 00:03:19.282
Take a look at what you just did.
[Lefkoe making skating sound effect]

00:03:21.659 --> 00:03:25.705
Ah, ooh. Woah, I almost bit…
- [DeBrincat laughing]

00:03:25.705 --> 00:03:28.374
- Bang, make it snappy.
- [DeBrincat chuckling]

00:03:28.374 --> 00:03:30.293
- [Lefkoe:] Bang.

00:03:30.293 --> 00:03:32.921
I'm not giving this back. I'm proud of you.

00:03:34.172 --> 00:03:36.216
That's the big X-factor.
- [DeBrincat:] All right, I'm keeping this in my pocket.

00:03:36.216 --> 00:03:38.218
- Yeah, tell Sidney Crosby to eat it.
- Yeah.

00:03:38.218 --> 00:03:38.885
- Perfect.

00:03:39.886 --> 00:03:42.430
- [Nasher:] So obviously, Alex
 is a smaller guy in the NHL,

00:03:42.472 --> 00:03:44.349
but he doesn't let that bring him down.

00:03:44.349 --> 00:03:46.267
He's able to utilize his speed

00:03:46.267 --> 00:03:49.938
and, of course, that ankle-breaker.
Make his way up the ice, quick

00:03:49.938 --> 00:03:51.648
move, can get the shot

00:03:51.648 --> 00:03:55.735
and we can bury the goal.
[Horn blowing, crowd cheering]

00:04:05.203 --> 00:04:07.247
♪♪♪
- All right. So you did phenomenal in the

00:04:07.247 --> 00:04:10.375
make it snappy, but now it is time
for the ankle-breaker drill.

00:04:10.667 --> 00:04:13.878
You're gonna go through.
I need to see quickness.

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:16.756
You can't lose speed,
but you gotta break some ankles.

00:04:17.173 --> 00:04:19.842
I'm not qualified to judge this.
Would you agree?

00:04:19.926 --> 00:04:21.719
- Yeah, I would agree.
- Oh, great, awesome.

00:04:21.719 --> 00:04:25.807
But I have someone that is: the greatest
that's ever done it,

00:04:26.266 --> 00:04:28.059
Wayne Gretzky, the Great One.
Bang.

00:04:30.061 --> 00:04:32.355
- Thank you. All right, let's
 see what you got. I'm so excited.

00:04:32.730 --> 00:04:34.315
- What are we looking for, Wayne?

00:04:34.315 --> 00:04:36.609
What are we, what are you looking for?

00:04:36.609 --> 00:04:40.697
Well, first of all, we want to look
for balance, and you have to have speed.

00:04:41.281 --> 00:04:44.450
That's a hard combination
to keep the balance and speed together.

00:04:44.867 --> 00:04:47.870
So if you can keep
the balance and the speed, you'll be fine.

00:04:48.162 --> 00:04:50.248
But it's a hard one.
This is a tough one to do.

00:04:50.248 --> 00:04:53.293
- Do you wanna ask any advice?

00:04:53.459 --> 00:04:56.546
Do you wanna say anything to him?

00:04:56.546 --> 00:04:58.339
- Uh, no, I think I'll just give it a go.

00:04:58.339 --> 00:04:59.549
- He's gonna give it a go.

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:01.467
Wayne, are you ready to judge?
- All right—

00:05:01.467 --> 00:05:03.052
- I don't want you to be soft.

00:05:03.052 --> 00:05:05.805
I want harsh criticism.
- All right, I will be.

00:05:05.805 --> 00:05:06.597
- Awesome.

00:05:06.597 --> 00:05:09.475
All right, Gretzky, let's do this. You got it, Cat.
- All right.

00:05:11.519 --> 00:05:13.688
All right, Cat. Keep the speed,

00:05:13.688 --> 00:05:15.898
break some ankles.
Whenever you're ready, man.

00:05:19.319 --> 00:05:22.655
Easy... easy work.
Easy work. Woo!

00:05:25.783 --> 00:05:27.869
Now I see why he was third in goals.

00:05:30.872 --> 00:05:31.831
Man, that was good.

00:05:31.831 --> 00:05:34.083
OK, let's go to the Great One.

00:05:34.083 --> 00:05:36.836
What did you think from what you saw?

00:05:36.836 --> 00:05:39.464
- Well, first of all,
 you guys brought in a ringer.

00:05:39.464 --> 00:05:40.798
His technique was really good.

00:05:40.798 --> 00:05:44.135
He was upright. He had balance.
He had great mobility.

00:05:44.469 --> 00:05:46.429
He was strong. He was fast.

00:05:46.429 --> 00:05:48.973
It was really good.
- Were the ankles broken?

00:05:49.015 --> 00:05:51.726
Like, if you were a defender,
would he have broken your ankles?

00:05:52.101 --> 00:05:53.728
- Well, I wasn't a very good defender.
- [Laughing]

00:05:53.728 --> 00:05:54.645
- So probably, right?

00:05:55.980 --> 00:05:59.192
- I was better going the other way.
- Yeah.

00:05:59.192 --> 00:06:01.277
- I really didn't do much backing up.

00:06:01.277 --> 00:06:03.654
We should move the cones,
make it harder for him.

00:06:04.155 --> 00:06:05.823
- How would you like to move them?

00:06:05.823 --> 00:06:08.576
-  My grandson could go through those cones.
- [Laughing]

00:06:08.576 --> 00:06:11.120
And he's five. And he lives in Florida.

00:06:11.120 --> 00:06:13.206
So you need to stagger the cones.

00:06:13.247 --> 00:06:15.124
So he has to kinda go in and out.

00:06:15.124 --> 00:06:19.420
That's how we're gonna see if he has
agility and balance together.

00:06:19.420 --> 00:06:20.838
- Stagger the cones.

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:23.007
When you speak, we listen.

00:06:23.007 --> 00:06:24.675
Move 'em! Move the cones!
- [Laughing]

00:06:24.675 --> 00:06:25.385
- Let's do it.
♪♪♪

00:06:31.849 --> 00:06:34.102
- [DeBrincat:] They're really making this tough on me.

00:06:34.102 --> 00:06:38.272
- Now we will see what he's really got.
 We need one more cone where he's standing.

00:06:38.856 --> 00:06:40.233
You know what, can we get

00:06:40.233 --> 00:06:42.610
one of you guys just to stand there?

00:06:42.610 --> 00:06:44.404
- Yeah?
- Yeah, you could stand there.

00:06:44.404 --> 00:06:46.989
- Oh, man. All right.

00:06:47.198 --> 00:06:49.283
- [Wayne Gretzky:] See? That's what a good host
 does. He's versatile.

00:06:49.742 --> 00:06:51.786
- [Lefkoe:] Wayne's making it tough, man.

00:06:51.786 --> 00:06:53.788
- You're the first cone. Here we go.
- You know,

00:06:53.871 --> 00:06:56.582
you know, for someone that said, "Oh,
he did a great job,"

00:06:56.749 --> 00:06:59.335
you really got a lot of suggestions with this one.

00:07:00.294 --> 00:07:02.380
- Well, I wanna see if he's really good.

00:07:02.380 --> 00:07:06.676
- OK, deal. We have the suggestions
 from the Great One.

00:07:07.093 --> 00:07:11.180
I am now a prop, and we are gonna
see the Cat in action.

00:07:11.180 --> 00:07:12.515
Whenever you're ready, man.

00:07:16.227 --> 00:07:20.982
♪♪♪
Wow, wow. Wow...

00:07:21.899 --> 00:07:29.490
Hey! And he drills

00:07:29.490 --> 00:07:31.993
the goalie in the face.

00:07:33.161 --> 00:07:36.539
- See?
- Come on. Come on, Wayne.

00:07:37.039 --> 00:07:40.126
- OK, he's really good.
And I knew he was good.

00:07:40.168 --> 00:07:42.128
That's why I wanted
 to make it more difficult.

00:07:42.128 --> 00:07:44.130
- Yeah.
- [Gretzky:] That was really good.

00:07:44.130 --> 00:07:46.340
He bent his shoulders down when he leaned in.

00:07:46.674 --> 00:07:48.801
Kept it up the other way
when he went the other way.

00:07:49.010 --> 00:07:51.679
He had his stick turned properly.

00:07:51.679 --> 00:07:54.182
I gotta tell you, it was really good.

00:07:54.182 --> 00:07:56.392
- [Lefkoe:] I just want to know,
 what is it like to hear that?

00:07:56.392 --> 00:07:59.729
- [DeBrincat:] That's crazy. I mean, obviously,
the Great One

00:07:59.729 --> 00:08:01.647
- [Lefkoe:] Yeah.
- telling you that,

00:08:01.647 --> 00:08:03.858
you know, shows you some accomplishment.
- Mm.

00:08:03.983 --> 00:08:06.486
- And hopefully I can get this ankle-breaker.
- I love it. All right.

00:08:06.486 --> 00:08:11.449
So now, Wayne, I'll ask you, in your mind
should he keep the ankle-breaker?

00:08:12.992 --> 00:08:16.329
- Yes. And you are a great pylon.
- [Laughing]

00:08:16.662 --> 00:08:19.081
- So this was a win-win.

00:08:19.081 --> 00:08:23.628
- You know, that's what I've been working to
 my entire life was for that moment. Wow.

00:08:23.836 --> 00:08:25.630
How 'bout that?
- It's crazy.

00:08:25.630 --> 00:08:26.547
- I, one,

00:08:27.298 --> 00:08:29.592
I was a little bit nervous
that you were gonna run me over.

00:08:29.634 --> 00:08:32.053
And now I experienced that speed firsthand.

00:08:33.221 --> 00:08:34.972
Tore up the drill.

00:08:34.972 --> 00:08:36.140
You keep the ankle-breaker.

00:08:36.140 --> 00:08:38.309
But that last compliment for me,

00:08:38.309 --> 00:08:40.478
I feel like that's something
that I would hold for a while.

00:08:40.478 --> 00:08:41.187
- Yeah, for sure.

00:08:41.479 --> 00:08:43.856
- Congratulations, bro.
- Thank you.

00:08:43.856 --> 00:08:45.775
- The Cat in action.
- [Laughing]

00:08:45.775 --> 00:08:47.985
- The claws are out.

00:08:47.985 --> 00:08:49.612
Man, he almost run me over, jeez.
♪♪♪

